Task: Your task is to implement polymorphism by overriding the `cast()` method in two specialized spell classes: `Fireball` and `IceShard`. Each spell should describe its unique magical effect when cast.

Submitted code:
```
class Spell {
    // 1. Store the name in a way that subclasses can access without parsing strings
    #name;

    constructor(name) {
        this.#name = name;
    }

    // 2. Add a getter so subclasses can use the name directly
    get name() {
        return this.#name;
    }

    cast() {
        return `${this.name} prepares to cast a generic spell.`;
    }
}

class Fireball extends Spell {
    constructor() {
        super("Fireball");
    }

    cast() {
        // Efficiency: No super.cast() call, no .split(), no array creation
        return `${this.name} unleashes a devastating inferno!`;
    }
}

class IceShard extends Spell {
    constructor() {
        super("Ice Shard");
    }

    cast() {
        // Cleanliness: Removed the redundant private helper and string slicing
        return `${this.name} summons a flurry of chilling ice shards.`;
    }
}

// --- Usage ---
const fireball = new Fireball();
const iceShard = new IceShard();

console.log(fireball.cast());
console.log(iceShard.cast());

```

Does this code correctly implement the polymorphism concept? Check for proper OOP usage.
